Copy this file, rename it to <slug>.md (lowercase, hyphens, no spaces) and
fill it in. The .md.example extension keeps this template itself out of the
site: the collection only loads *.md files.

Required: name, slug, city, country, address, lat, lng, source, context.
Optional: rank, note, signatureCocktail, relatedIngredients, image.

Getting lat/lng: open https://www.openstreetmap.org, search the address,
right click the spot and choose "Show address". The coordinates appear in
the left panel. Six decimal places is plenty. Both must be plain numbers,
not quoted strings, or the build will fail. A bar without valid coordinates
is not plotted on the map.

---
name: Bar Name
slug: bar-name
city: Hamburg
country: Germany
address: "Full street address as published"

# Numbers, not strings. Southern hemisphere lat and western hemisphere lng
# are negative.
lat: 53.550341
lng: 9.992196

# Where the facts in `context` come from. For a bar you went to yourself,
# name yourself and the date, e.g.
# "Visited by Simon Engel, March 2026"
source: "Visited by Simon Engel, March 2026"

# Only for entries on The World's 50 Best Bars. Delete this line otherwise:
# an unranked bar renders without the brass rank badge.
rank: 12

# The sourced description. Everything here must trace to `source` above.
# Keep the register dry and understated, per CLAUDE.md rule 4.
context: >-
  What the place is, who runs it, what the programme is built on. Facts, not
  adjectives.

# Your own comment. Optional, and the one field where opinion belongs.
# Renders under a brass "From the visit" label, separated from the cited
# description so the two are never confused.
note: >-
  What you actually thought. What you drank, who you went with, whether the
  room worked.

# Delete this whole block if the bar has no single signature drink. Do not
# invent one. Three of the seeded bars omit it for exactly this reason.
signatureCocktail:
  name: Drink Name
  description: >-
    What is in it and what it is doing.

# Any of ube, yuzu, matcha. Each renders as a link to that chapter page.
# Leave as [] if the bar has no genuine connection to one of the three.
relatedIngredients: []

# Optional. Delete the whole block if there is no photo.
# CLAUDE.md rule 5: every image is either AI generated or properly credited,
# never uncaptioned.
#   credit: ai-generated   -> caption is suffixed "AI generated."
#   credit: photographer   -> `attribution` is shown instead, and is required
image:
  src: /images/bars/bar-name.jpg
  alt: Describe what is in the frame, for screen readers.
  caption: Short caption.
  credit: photographer
  attribution: "Photo: Simon Engel"
---
